WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.300
- Today on Drew, take a deep
dive into the season one.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.980
- I'm so in awe that
we're all still so close,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.410
we've experienced everything together.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.780
- [Announcer] And we gear
up for our star study,

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.700
two weeks premier event.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.910
- In my original hometown of Hollywood.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.300
I grew up here in Los
Angeles, I love it here.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.163
It all starts now.

00:00:25.163 --> 00:00:27.746
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.920
- [Announcer] Please
welcome Drew Barrymore.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.260
- Hi everyone, the countdown
is for season two premiere.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.020
of the Drew Barry Marchelle.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.500
It's less than a week away.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.110
And the first thing we're
gonna do is show our undying

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.030
appreciation for all of our hometowns.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.810
I'm gonna start in my
hometown of Los Angeles.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.340
But before we do that,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.110
let's take a look back at how we got here.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.370
These are our favorite
moments from season one,

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.780
and we curated them just for you.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.330
We kicked off the season
premiere with two women that

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:12.200
I just, well, they're
my nearest and dearest.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.620
That first guest is a
really important thing

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.230
in the talk show world,
and I actually said,

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.300
could I have my friends on?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.480
You might happen to know
who they are, ironically,

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.480
it's Cameron Diaz and Lucy Lu,
my fellow Charlie's Angels.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.643
Take a look.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.380
We all made Charlie's Angels.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.700
We made it and we're making this show.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.890
And so when we sat around
and thought about who is this

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.060
you know, first guest?

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.280
Nothing felt right, nothing was there.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.620
And all of the sudden in
like a divine intervention,

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.130
I was like Cameron and Lucy,

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.930
and everything fell into place.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.125
- Massive, congratulations,
this is really major for you.

00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:00.740
(audience applauding)

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.260
- Listen, you know, everybody says,

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.980
who's gonna be your first guest.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.760
It's like, I mean, we've been
through everything together.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.138
- Well, everything.

00:02:11.138 --> 00:02:12.589
- Everything.

00:02:12.589 --> 00:02:14.313
- Literally everything.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.850
- I haven't had a wedding
that you guys haven't been at.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.580
- I've been to all your weddings,
I've been to all of them.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.070
- Like when our babies are born,

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.150
we hang out and we do
the birthday party thing.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.530
I can't believe we're all moms now.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.390
That's when I got really emotional.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:41.900
First, I sent Cameron
a video and I'm saying,

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.560
Hey, listen, I got it like,

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.090
I wanna ask you something
when you come on the show,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:51.070
which, I mean, I've never
done this in my life

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.500
because I'm so comfortable.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.600
I mean, we have lived
together all over the world.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.540
So of course, to save time,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.240
I sent her a video while
I'm getting dressed

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.810
and you don't see anything,
I'm not that dumb,

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.260
but I'm getting out of the shower

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.750
and I'm like wringing out of my towel.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.650
And I don't hear back from
her for like two days.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.063
And I'm like, this is weird.

00:03:12.502 --> 00:03:13.335
What is going on?

00:03:13.335 --> 00:03:16.290
So I text her and I'm like, I
don't care about the question.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.490
Are you okay?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.600
I don't hear again for two
days and I'm freaking out.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.400
So I call her and I'm
like, what is going on?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.000
I'm worried, is everything okay?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.550
She's like, I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.960
I'm like the video.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.040
You didn't get my video?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.728
Turns out a young boy

00:03:33.728 --> 00:03:34.833
got the video.

00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:35.666
(laughs)

00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:37.305
- Lucky him. Oh no.

00:03:37.305 --> 00:03:38.690
- Oh, no.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.390
- Oh, no, by the way, it's
like seven minutes long.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:42.223
- Oh, my God.

00:03:43.331 --> 00:03:45.623
(laughs)

00:03:45.623 --> 00:03:46.456
- It's like epic.

00:03:46.456 --> 00:03:47.770
I mean, this is some material-

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:48.980
- Secret revealed.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.740
- Material for like,

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.112
honestly, this is gonna last
him three or four years.

00:03:54.112 --> 00:03:55.220
(laughs)

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.460
- I mean, I'm really like hamming it up

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.770
because it's, you know-

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:00.670
- 'Cause it's you.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.850
- I was like, send me
that video immediately.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.990
I need to know what is in that video.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.457
And the whole while I'm just
like cracking up because-

00:04:10.457 --> 00:04:12.270
- You need to send me this video as well,

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.510
or do it through someone
else because I didn't get

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:15.820
your other video either.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:16.770
- So then I said...

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.380
No, something's wrong with my phone.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.510
So I sent Lucy this video crying,

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.150
inviting her on the show saying-

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.790
- In her bathroom crying.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.623
- I'm in my bathroom.

00:04:27.623 --> 00:04:28.456
- She was dressed.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.490
- I was fully clothed at this time.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:35.350
I didn't take the risk and she
didn't get the video either.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.870
- Come on.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.383
- I know, I know.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:44.500
The thing that I love about
our friendship is that

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.260
we have been there in all the
big and important moments.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.450
We've also been there in the small moments

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.110
and the casual moments.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.290
And the reason we are such good friends

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.130
is because it's real.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.410
And we go through real
stuff with each other.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.943
It's not a Hollywood fairytale.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.100
- There's no aspect of life

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.750
that's an actual Hollywood fairytale.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.060
That's why it's a Hollywood fairytale

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.110
'cause it doesn't exist.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.050
It's aspirational, it's hopeful,

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.630
but life is constantly
full of twists and turns

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.410
and all those things that
happen over a lifetime,

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.980
because truly it is now a lifetime.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:28.010
I mean, 20 years is a long time y'all.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.680
Like, I'm two years away from 50.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.330
You know, that's nearly half my life.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.750
We have Charlie's Angels
as our sort of backdrop

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.140
that brought us together.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:44.500
But then we get to fill
in all of life together

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.033
and real moments, which I
just so appreciate, so much.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.590
- It's so true.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.760
- It's so well said to me.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.593
- I know.

00:05:50.593 --> 00:05:53.110
- Because it's like, it's
our touch point, you know?

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.620
But then we have that foundation
and then we've obviously

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.600
grown and learned and changed.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.200
And I mean, I know that
20 years has gone by,

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.120
but I feel like it was yesterday.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.370
I feel just as fresh and
as young and as you know,

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.660
creatively, I don't know,
excited as I was when I started.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.473
- Here's the thing about Charlie's Angels,

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.600
is that it's about girls who
can do all of these things

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.130
and love each other.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:25.460
And don't have competition and
support each other and laugh

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:29.580
and wanna talk about love
and life so much that they

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.490
actually start to talk about loving life

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.350
while they're fighting,

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.310
because women are so like
that at all intersect.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:38.090
And that is why I asked
you guys here today,

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.950
is because if you're
gonna do something big,

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.450
you wanna do it with your girlfriends.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.662
- That's right.

00:06:44.662 --> 00:06:47.829
(audience applauding)

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:51.440
And I love being together.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.660
Although are we really together?

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.100
Are we all together in this room?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:57.933
- Are we?

00:06:57.933 --> 00:07:01.743
I feel like we're connected
in some way, but maybe.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.670
- For anyone watching,

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:09.061
can you guess which one
of us isn't really here?

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:11.515
(dramatic music)

00:07:11.515 --> 00:07:14.484
(gasping)

00:07:14.484 --> 00:07:15.747
Welcome back.

00:07:15.747 --> 00:07:18.163
- I'm the one in Los Angeles.

00:07:19.094 --> 00:07:22.000
(laughing)

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.370
You gotta try this, it's so incredible.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.070
The ether, the little
particles going out into space

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:30.960
and coming back and remapping
into this beautiful space.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.620
You guys, it's crazy, you should try it.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:33.691
It tingles.

00:07:33.691 --> 00:07:35.774
(laughs)

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.600
(audience applauding)

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.500
- All right, we're not
done yet with those ladies,

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:45.067
more with Cameron and Lucy up next.

00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:47.650
(upbeat music)

00:07:52.567 --> 00:07:54.435
♪ If you're into fashion ♪

00:07:54.435 --> 00:07:57.221
♪ Or easy home decor ♪

00:07:57.221 --> 00:07:59.500
♪ New favorite recipes ♪

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.853
♪ Plus fun celebrities ♪

00:08:01.853 --> 00:08:03.850
♪ With a little good news ♪

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.275
We're back to bring you more.

00:08:06.275 --> 00:08:10.967
♪ Barrymore, choose a
little for season two ♪

00:08:10.967 --> 00:08:15.582
♪ Yeah, Barrymore, life
improving, stain removing ♪

00:08:15.582 --> 00:08:18.100
♪ Barrymore ♪

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.390
- [Announcer] The new season of Drew,

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.903
premiere September 13th.

00:08:25.051 --> 00:08:27.634
(upbeat music)

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.790
- Welcome back, we just
showed our premiere interview

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:37.790
with my nearest and dearest,
Cameron Diaz and Lucy Lou.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.560
Later in that episode,

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:44.299
the three of us dove
into our ongoing roles,

00:08:44.299 --> 00:08:47.810
(sighs) as moms, take a look.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:52.810
So we grew and we grew
up and now we are moms.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:57.550
Do you think you're a person
now Lucy, than you were then?

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.960
Like, aside from us knowing
each other and our friendship,

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.210
just you as a human?

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:05.930
- I think in my twenties,
I felt very Bulletproof

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:10.480
and very I don't wanna
say it was risk-taking

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.380
'cause it was beyond that.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:14.220
It was like, I didn't really
care if I lived or died.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.320
I just didn't and I lost
my father a few years ago

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:21.150
and I didn't really recognize the levels

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.890
that we have in our lives.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:27.890
And like he was a place in my life that

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:33.020
was always sort of kind
of a roof, you know?

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.670
And so suddenly you feel like

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.010
the roof has been torn off and
then you sort of recognize,

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.090
oh, I am now the roof,

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:42.360
and I happen to have a child,

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.930
so I guess I'm the roof to that child.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.420
So now I really have to understand that

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:50.030
I have to shelter him and
I have a responsibility.

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.300
And it's a very powerful thing.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.950
It's also terrifying, if I think about it

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.860
I think my heart was smaller back then,

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:00.320
'cause it was sort of more
inclined to what I wanted to do.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.490
But now it's sort of like,
what do we want to do?

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:06.660
And it feels good because I
feel like a fuller person.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.750
Like life seems a much more, you know,

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:13.640
kind of colorful and wild
because there's so many more

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.910
opportunities as a mom
to kind of like discover.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:21.350
And there's so much
more curiosity with kids

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.280
and it's mind blowing and
it's actually more terrifying

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:25.410
in a way, you know,

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.560
because you're also responsible
for this little person.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.393
- Highest stake.

00:10:28.393 --> 00:10:30.580
- So it's like, oh my
God, I thought I was on

00:10:31.567 --> 00:10:33.300
a ride back then, a wild ride.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:36.260
But actually it's now that
it's even more intense.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.930
- Well, you nailed it because
you're just dealing with

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.290
your own mortality.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.290
And all of the sudden when you have a kid,

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.050
I don't care if it sounds co-dependent,

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:47.120
my kids are more meaningful
to me than my own life.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.020
- I think there's
something that in our DNA

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.150
that gets triggered, you know,

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:57.150
like that just clicks on
when you become a parent.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:01.430
You have to make sure that they survive.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.710
They go on you, we will die.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:06.100
I'm sorry to get like morbid,

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.000
and this is those times when Drew goes

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:12.050
bear, really you're gonna die?

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.276
Do we have to talk about that?

00:11:14.276 --> 00:11:15.860
- But your first show
was all about mortality.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:19.246
- I know, I think I'm
ready to about death.

00:11:19.246 --> 00:11:22.500
I think I'm no longer a young idiot

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.540
who thinks I am immortal,
which I'm glad to know I'm not,

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:26.770
I wasn't the only one.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.410
I mean, I heard myself around,

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.600
I abused this carcass to no end

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.340
and I just thought Drew,
I was gonna die young.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.170
So who cares, live now and go for it.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:41.060
And now, yeah, I mean, 2020 will make you

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:42.270
think about your mortality.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.480
Children will make you think
about where your mortality.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:47.380
- Yeah, in my twenties it was
just sort of like, here we go.

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:48.450
Yeah, all right.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.800
Yep, jump on that.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:52.200
Gotcha, oh, is that a wild horse?

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:55.330
Oh, cool, yeah, no, I know
how to hold on for my life.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.770
Let's go.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:59.863
- There's such a liberation
in that too though.

00:12:00.911 --> 00:12:02.070
- Yeah, I'm so glad I did it all.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:06.870
- When I thought about trying
to accomplish something big

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.490
in my life at another point,

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.060
you two were the people I did it with.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:14.170
And so of course, what a natural fit

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.670
that you're the two people that came into

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.830
my head and my heart when I thought,

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:23.690
how would I like to honor this endeavor?

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.760
I see myself with you guys.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:30.080
- I feel like it's exactly
what the world needs.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:33.250
They need your light,
they need your joyousness.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.640
They need your perspective.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:40.160
One of the things that I have
always been in total awe of

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.470
in you, is your ability to like
take in all the information,

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:48.020
how quick you are to not just
like what's in front of you,

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:51.110
but like the nuances and the sort of,

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.750
the humanity and intellect.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.223
You read more books
than any person I know.

00:12:57.306 --> 00:13:01.417
You listen to more music,
you look at more art,

00:13:02.777 --> 00:13:05.710
